      "type": "concept",
      "codeLanguage": "javascript",
      "summary": "ការការពារសុវត្ថិភាព Cookies (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)៖\n\n- **httpOnly**៖ ទប់ស្កាត់ការលួច Token តាមរយៈ JavaScript និង XSS Attacks។\n- **secure**៖ បង្ខំឱ្យ Browser បញ្ជូន Cookie តែតាមបណ្តាញ HTTPS ប៉ុណ្ណោះ។\n- **sameSite**៖ កំណត់ `'strict'` ឬ `'lax'` ដើម្បីការពារការវាយប្រហារ Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)។",
      "tip": "Use `SameSite=Lax` for standard web apps where users might follow external links to your site, or `SameSite=Strict` for sensitive single-page APIs.",
      "objective": "Master the triumvirate of cookie security flags: HttpOnly, Secure, and SameSite.",
      "expectedOutcome": "Cookies that cannot be hijacked by XSS or forged by cross-origin CSRF attacks.",
      "codeSnippet": "// Express Cookie Security Best Practice:\nres.cookie(\"token\", value, {\n  httpOnly: true,                         // Defeats XSS (No JS access)\n  secure: process.env.NODE_ENV === \"production\", // Defeats Sniffing (HTTPS only)\n  sameSite: \"strict\",                    // Defeats CSRF (Never sent cross-site)\n  domain: \".myenterprise.com\",           // Restrict to trusted subdomains\n  path: \"/\",\n  maxAge: 3600000,                       // 1 hour\n});"
