      "tip": "Install `express-mongo-sanitize` and mount it globally to automatically strip `$` operators from `req.body`, `req.query`, and `req.params`.",
      "objective": "Identify NoSQL injection mechanics and deploy automated sanitization middleware.",
      "expectedOutcome": "Complete immunity against MongoDB operator injection attacks.",
      "codeSnippet": "import mongoSanitize from \"express-mongo-sanitize\";\n\n// Attack scenario if unsanitized:\n// Attacker sends POST body: { \"email\": \"admin@app.com\", \"password\": { \"$ne\": null } }\n// MongoDB interprets: Find admin where password is not null -> LOGIN BYPASSED!\n\n// Defense: Mount express-mongo-sanitize\n// Replaces prohibited characters ($, .) with underscores or removes them entirely\napp.use(mongoSanitize());\n\n// Also enforce strict string schemas with Zod:\nconst loginSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  password: z.string().min(1), // Rejects objects like {\"$ne\": null} with 400 Bad Request!\n});"
