      "summary": "យុទ្ធសាស្ត្រជ្រើសរើសទីតាំងផ្ទុកឯកសារ (Local vs Cloud Storage)៖\n\n- **Local Disk Storage**៖ សមស្របសម្រាប់តែដំណាក់កាល Development ព្រោះមិនអាច Scale លើ Multi-instance Containers បាន។\n- **Cloud Object Storage (S3-Compatible)**៖ ស្តង់ដារ Production ដោយសារ Scalability គ្មានដែនកំណត់, ភាពធន់ខ្ពស់, និង CDN Integration។\n- **Stateless Server Principle**៖ រក្សា Server ឱ្យនៅជា Stateless ដោយមិនពឹងផ្អែកលើ Local Hard Disk ឡើយ។",
      "tip": "Never store production user uploads on the ephemeral local container filesystem. Always use object storage like S3 or R2 for production backends.",
      "objective": "Evaluate trade-offs between local filesystem storage and cloud object stores.",
      "expectedOutcome": "Architectural strategy suited for stateless, scalable container deployments.",
      "codeSnippet": "// Comparison Matrix:\n// Feature            | Local Disk Storage       | Cloud Object Storage (S3/R2)\n// -------------------+--------------------------+------------------------------\n// Setup Complexity   | Zero (built-in)          | Requires cloud credentials & SDK\n// Scalability        | Limited to server disk   | Infinite, virtually unlimited\n// Docker Containers  | Ephemeral (Lost on reboot)| Persistent & stateless\n// Global CDN         | Needs reverse proxy setup| Built-in CDN edge distribution\n// Backup/Durability  | Manual backups required  | 99.999999999% (11 9s) durability"
