      "khmerTitle": "លំហូរ Password Reset ជាមួយ Cryptographic Token",
      "type": "lab",
      "codeLanguage": "javascript",
      "summary": "លំហូរ Password Reset ជាមួយ Cryptographic Token៖\n\n- **Generate Crypto Token**៖ បង្កើត Random Token តាមរយៈ `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex')`។\n- **Hash & Save with Expiry**៖ Hash Token រួចរក្សាទុកក្នុង MongoDB ជាមួយកាលបរិច្ឆេទផុតកំណត់ (10 នាទី)។\n- **Send Reset Link**៖ ផ្ញើ Reset URL ដែលមានផ្ទុក Unhashed Token តាមរយៈ Email ទៅកាន់ User។\n- **Verify & Update**៖ នៅពេល User ចុច Link Server Hash Token មកផ្ទៀងផ្ទាត់ជាមួយ Database មុននឹងអនុញ្ញាតឱ្យប្តូរ Password ថ្មី។",
      "tip": "Never store the raw reset token in your database! Hash it with SHA-256 before saving, exactly like passwords, so a database leak doesn't permit account takeovers.",
      "objective": "Implement a secure password reset workflow using hashed tokens and time limits.",
      "expectedOutcome": "Cryptographically sound forgot/reset password system.",
      "codeSnippet": "import crypto from \"node:crypto\";\n\n// 1. Generate reset token in User Model method:\nuserSchema.methods.createPasswordResetToken = function () {\n  const resetToken = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString(\"hex\");\n\n  // Hash token before saving to database\n  this.passwordResetToken = crypto\n    .createHash(\"sha256\")\n    .update(resetToken)\n    .digest(\"hex\");\n\n  // Token expires in 10 minutes\n  this.passwordResetExpires = Date.now() + 10 * 60 * 1000;\n\n  return resetToken; // Return unhashed token to send via email\n};\n\n// 2. Controller sends reset link:\nconst resetUrl = `${process.env.CLIENT_URL}/reset-password?token=${resetToken}`;"
